    Bug 2051601 - Port bug 2046258 - Adapt mailnews to the async nsIPKCS11Token API and nsNSSHelper.h removal. r=thunderbird-reviewers,edicharry,kaie

    Bug 2046258 made nsIPKCS11Token's login(), logout(), reset() and
    changePassword() asynchronous (they now take a JSContext and return a
    Promise) and removed nsNSSHelper.h (PipUIContext and getNSSDialogs).

    S/MIME (nsNSSHelper.h removal):
    - nsCMS.cpp, nsCMSSecureMessage.cpp, nsMsgComposeSecure.cpp,
      nsCertPicker.cpp: drop the nsNSSHelper.h include.
    - Replace PipUIContext with a null nsIInterfaceRequestor; the NSS
      password callback was already null at these call sites, so NSS falls
      back to its registered global callback.
    - nsCertPicker.cpp: replace getNSSDialogs() with do_GetService(), as
      done on the m-c side.

    Async login:
    - nsMsgDBFolder::PromptForMasterPasswordIfNecessary() must stay
      synchronous (it is called from synchronous folder code), so it now
      drives the Promise returned by Login() and spins the event loop until
      it settles. The underlying PK11_Authenticate runs off the main thread,
      so the loop stays responsive.
    - qrExport.mjs and passwordManager.js: await logout()/login().
    - browser_qrExport.js and browser_policy_disable_masterpassword.js:
      await changePassword().

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309590

